[gd_scene load_steps=51 format=3]

; Merchant model for Yetannia -- animated flipbook.
; Generated by .tools/build-alt-scenes.py -- do not hand-edit; retune the script instead.
;
; BASE-LIB CONTRACT: NMerchantCharacterFactory has no named-node requirements and keeps this
; scene root as child #0 of the generated NMerchantCharacter, ON TOP OF copying that root's
; Scale onto the generated node -- so the root's scale is 1 here and Visuals carries the
; character scale (vanilla's merchant scenes have the same shape: root Node2D, no scale;
; the visual child carries 0.47). With the scale on the root the figure is drawn at 2.01x
; too large, head above the screen. NMerchantCharacter._Ready wraps
; GetChild(0) in `new MegaSprite(...)`, which THROWS for anything but a SpineSprite, and stock
; Godot has no SpineSprite -- so YetanniaPatches skips that call and plays this AnimationPlayer
; instead (idle on ready, 'die' at the game-over screen), which also removes the ERROR the mod
; used to log on every shop visit. POSITION/POSE ARE AN APPROXIMATION: no shopkeeper clip
; exists in the source data; this is the standing idle.
;
; The atlas is the SAME texture the in-combat flipbook uses, so this scene adds no texture memory;
; it only adds AtlasTexture regions and an Animation.

